.\" Adapted from kbd 2.10.0 docs/man/man1/loadkeys.1, GPL-2.0-or-later.
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt LOADKEYS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm loadkeys
.Nd load console keyboard maps
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a b c d h m p q s u v V
.Op Fl Fl tkeymap Ns Op = Ns Ar shape
.Op Fl C Ar console
.Op Ar map ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
loads text keymaps, function strings and compose definitions into the
console keyboard.
Maps are read in order, so an overlay can change selected entries of a layout.
With no map operand, input comes from standard input.
Named maps are sought under
.Pa /usr/share/kbd/keymaps ;
the suffix
.Pa .map
may be omitted.
.Pp
.Fl u
loads Unicode entries.
On Rach2 it leaves raw and mediumraw keyboard modes unchanged, so a running
terminal can continue reading keycodes during a load.
A failed load can leave part of the map changed; reload a known map to recover.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Force conversion to the current 8-bit character set.
.It Fl b
Write a binary keymap to standard output instead of changing the keyboard.
This form omits function strings and compose definitions.
.It Fl c
Clear the compose table before loading the definitions.
.It Fl C Ar console
Use this console device.
.It Fl d
Load the default map.
.It Fl m
Write C source describing the map instead of changing the keyboard.
.It Fl p
Find and parse the maps without applying them.
.It Fl Fl tkeymap Ns Op = Ns Ar shape
Write the combined text keymap to standard output instead of applying it.
The output shapes are those of
.Xr dumpkeys 1 .
.It Fl q
Suppress progress output.
.It Fl s
Clear the function strings before loading the definitions.
.It Fl u
Force Unicode conversion.
.It Fl v
Print more detail; may be repeated.
.It Fl h
Print help.
.It Fl V
Print the version.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
loadkeys -u kg alt-shift caps-ctrl
loadkeys -u us
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dumpkeys 1 ,
.Xr kbd_mode 1 ,
.Xr vconsole.conf 5
